bd4ff823-bde1-4b23-9125-78d7e5851485	a7000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000016	Describe a situation where you had to work outside your comfort zone.	STAR Framework:\n**Situation:** What was unfamiliar territory? (new domain, new role, new technology)\n**Task:** Why couldn't you stay in your comfort zone?\n**Action:** How did you prepare? What support did you seek? How did you manage the discomfort?\n**Result:** What did you achieve? How did it expand your capabilities?\n\nKey points: Show growth mindset, willingness to be uncomfortable, and effective self-management.\nGerman context: Show Eigeninitiative (self-initiative) in seeking knowledge and support.\n	\N	\N	MEDIUM	["behavioral", "adaptability", "growth"]	NEW	2.5	0	0	\N	2026-07-26 01:26:50.008137	0
c7689bb7-8bbe-4549-9895-c998fb9b97bc	a7000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000016	Tell me about a time shifting priorities forced you to reprioritize your work.	STAR Framework:\n**Situation:** What caused the priority shift? (business need, emergency, strategy change)\n**Task:** What work was in progress that needed deprioritization?\n**Action:** How did you decide what to pause/stop? How did you communicate the change?\n**Result:** Was the new priority delivered? What happened to the deprioritized work?\n\nKey points: Show pragmatic prioritization, clear communication, and no resentment about changing plans.\nGerman context: Show Flexibilität combined with Transparenz — adapt but communicate impact to all stakeholders.\n	\N	\N	EASY	["behavioral", "adaptability", "prioritization"]	NEW	2.5	0	0	\N	2026-07-26 01:26:50.011418	0
c05b315a-556e-49a1-b479-dcce520ee6e1	a7000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000015	Tell me about a time you explained a complex technical concept to a non-technical person.	STAR Framework:\n**Situation:** Who was the audience? What did they need to understand? Why?\n**Task:** What was at stake if they didn't understand? (budget approval, prioritization)\n**Action:** What analogies/visualizations did you use? How did you check understanding?\n**Result:** Did they make an informed decision? Did they feel confident in the direction?\n\nKey points: Show ability to adapt language to audience, use analogies, and verify comprehension.\nGerman context: Non-technical stakeholders often have engineering backgrounds. Don't oversimplify — be precise but accessible.\n	\N	\N	EASY	["behavioral", "communication", "simplification"]	NEW	2.5	0	0	\N	2026-07-26 01:26:50.018485	0
e50dcf61-dfcf-4dab-871e-ee28a74e290f	a7000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000015	Describe a time you gave difficult feedback to a peer.	STAR Framework:\n**Situation:** What behavior/output needed feedback? What was the impact?\n**Task:** Why was it your responsibility to give this feedback?\n**Action:** How did you deliver it? (private, specific examples, impact statements, suggestions)\n**Result:** How did the person respond? Did behavior change?\n\nKey points: Show courage, specificity, and care for the person's growth. Use SBI model (Situation-Behavior-Impact).\nGerman context: Direct feedback is normal and expected. Show Sachlichkeit — focus on behavior, not personality.\n	\N	\N	MEDIUM	["behavioral", "communication", "feedback"]	NEW	2.5	0	0	\N	2026-07-26 01:26:50.022696	0
0f6e6fd5-7827-4991-ae98-c39b176035e7	a7000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000015	Tell me about a time you had to present a technical proposal to senior leadership.	STAR Framework:\n**Situation:** What was the proposal? Who was the audience?\n**Task:** What decision did you need from them?\n**Action:** How did you structure the presentation? (problem → solution → cost → timeline → risks)\n**Result:** Was the proposal approved? What questions challenged your thinking?\n\nKey points: Show ability to communicate at executive level — business impact, not technical details.\nGerman context: German leadership values Entscheidungsvorlagen (decision templates). Present options with clear recommendation.\n	\N	\N	HARD	["behavioral", "communication", "stakeholder-management"]	NEW	2.5	0	0	\N	2026-07-26 01:26:50.028881	0
57c5f324-b67e-401f-a55f-9438ac110d0e	a7000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000015	Describe a situation where miscommunication caused a project problem.	STAR Framework:\n**Situation:** What was miscommunicated? Between whom?\n**Task:** What was the project impact?\n**Action:** How did you identify the miscommunication? How did you resolve it? What did you put in place to prevent recurrence?\n**Result:** Was the project recovered? What communication improvement stuck?\n\nKey points: Show ownership of communication failures, even if you weren't the root cause.\nGerman context: Show you implemented structural fixes (written specs, ADRs, meeting minutes) not just "we'll talk more."\n	\N	\N	MEDIUM	["behavioral", "communication", "miscommunication"]	NEW	2.5	0	0	\N	2026-07-26 01:26:50.033556	0
