54c806ab-081f-4ebd-81ce-6fe979be6fc9	a5000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000016	How does eventual consistency work in Cassandra and how do you tune it?	Cassandra replicates writes to N nodes asynchronously. Consistency level (CL) controls how many replicas must acknowledge before returning. CL=ONE gives fastest writes but stale reads. CL=QUORUM (majority) on both read and write guarantees strong consistency. Read-repair and anti-entropy repair reconcile divergent replicas in the background.\n	// Java driver consistency tuning\nSimpleStatement stmt = SimpleStatement.newInstance(\n    "SELECT * FROM orders WHERE user_id = ?", userId)\n    .setConsistencyLevel(DefaultConsistencyLevel.QUORUM);\nsession.execute(stmt);\n	\N	MEDIUM	["cassandra", "eventual-consistency", "tunable-consistency"]	NEW	2.5	0	0	\N	2026-07-26 00:49:24.981958	0
