5b21fd38-8bff-4ab6-bf11-079207cfa070	a4000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000012	Explain Manacher's algorithm for finding the longest palindromic substring in O(n).	Manacher's transforms the string by inserting separators (e.g., '#') to unify odd/even cases, then computes a radius array P[i] representing the palindrome radius at each center. It maintains a rightmost palindrome boundary and its center. For each new position, it mirrors a previously computed radius if within bounds, then expands. Each character is visited at most twice, yielding O(n) time. The longest palindromic substring has length max(P[i]) - 1.	\N	Key insight: palindromes within a larger palindrome have mirror symmetry, so previously computed radii can be reused rather than recomputing from scratch.	HARD	["manacher", "palindrome", "linear-time"]	NEW	2.5	0	0	\N	2026-07-26 00:49:25.143287	0
