ned by conversation_id; Cassandra or HBase for write throughput\n- Receipts: Delivered when gateway ACKs; read when recipient opens conversation\n- Push: If user offline >30s, trigger push notification via APNS/FCM\n	MEDIUM	50	2026-07-25 23:56:50.226147
aebcf7de-3c12-43ed-94bb-5e163e755047	a3000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000015	Design YouTube/Netflix	Design a video streaming platform that handles video upload, processing, storage, and adaptive streaming to millions of concurrent viewers.\n\n## Requirements\n\n### Functional\n- Upload videos (up to 4K resolution, max 12 hours)\n- Transcode videos into multiple resolutions and formats\n- Adaptive bitrate streaming based on viewer's bandwidth\n- Video recommendations and search\n- Comments, likes, and view tracking\n- Live streaming support\n\n### Non-Functional\n- Video playback start under 2 seconds\n- Support 100M concurrent streams\n- 99.99% availability for video playback\n- Upload processing within 30 minutes for a 1-hour video\n- Global low-latency delivery\n\n## Topics to Cover\n- Video transcoding pipeline and format selection\n- Adaptive bitrate streaming (HLS/DASH)\n- CDN architecture for video delivery\n- Storage tiering (hot/warm/cold)\n- Recommendation engine architecture\n	- 500M DAU, 100M concurrent streams at peak\n- 500 hours of video uploaded per minute\n- Average video: 10 minutes, 5 transcoded versions (240p to 4K)\n- Storage: ~1PB new video data per day\n- CDN: serve from edge within 50ms of viewer\n- Bandwidth: 5Mbps average per stream = 500 Tbps total\n	{"scalability": 20, "cdn_strategy": 15, "storage_design": 15, "video_pipeline": 25, "streaming_architecture": 25}	- Upload: Chunked upload to object store; metadata to DB; trigger transcoding pipeline\n- Transcoding: DAG-based pipeline — split video into segments, transcode in parallel, merge\n- Formats: HLS/DASH with segments at 240p, 480p, 720p, 1080p, 4K; multiple audio tracks\n- Streaming: Client requests manifest → selects quality based on bandwidth → fetches segments\n- CDN: Multi-tier — edge PoPs cache popular content; origin pull for long-tail\n- Storage: Hot (SSD, recent/popular) → Warm (HDD, older) → Cold (archival, rarely accessed)\n- Recommendations: Collaborative filtering + watch history; precomputed candidate lists\n- Live: Ingest via RTMP → segment in real-time → push to CDN edge; 5-15s latency\n- API: POST /videos/upload; GET /videos/{id}/manifest; GET /recommendations\n	MEDIUM	55	2026-07-25 23:56:50.228548
