tle, artist, album, lyrics\n- Offline: Download encrypted tracks to device; DRM license check on playback; sync delta on reconnect\n- API: GET /tracks/{id}/stream; GET /playlists/{id}; GET /recommendations/daily-mix\n	MEDIUM	50	2026-07-25 23:56:50.230929
6eaa7375-1597-4bfb-9948-83f7a372e652	a3000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000012	Design an API Rate Limiter	Design a distributed rate limiting service that protects APIs from abuse by enforcing request quotas per client across multiple server instances.\n\n## Requirements\n\n### Functional\n- Enforce rate limits per API key, user, or IP address\n- Support multiple rate limit rules (e.g., 100/min AND 5000/hour)\n- Return appropriate headers (X-RateLimit-Remaining, Retry-After)\n- Allow different limits per subscription tier (free, pro, enterprise)\n- Provide a dashboard showing usage and throttled requests\n\n### Non-Functional\n- Decision latency under 1ms (inline with request path)\n- Consistent enforcement across distributed servers\n- Graceful handling of Redis/store failures (fail-open vs fail-closed configurable)\n- Minimal memory footprint per client\n\n## Topics to Cover\n- Rate limiting algorithms (token bucket, sliding window, leaky bucket)\n- Distributed counter synchronization\n- Race condition handling in concurrent environments\n- Failure modes and degradation strategies\n	- 100K API clients, 1M requests/second total\n- Decision latency: under 1ms added to request\n- Rules: up to 5 rate limit rules per client\n- Distributed: 50 API gateway instances sharing state\n- Memory: under 1KB per client for rate limit state\n	{"api_design": 20, "performance": 15, "algorithm_choice": 25, "failure_handling": 15, "distributed_consistency": 25}	- Algorithm: Sliding window log for accuracy; token bucket for simplicity and memory efficiency\n- Storage: Redis with atomic Lua scripts for check-and-decrement in single round-trip\n- Distributed sync: Redis as central counter; local cache with sync for ultra-low latency\n- Race conditions: Redis MULTI/EXEC or Lua script ensures atomic read-check-update\n- Multiple rules: Evaluate all rules; reject if ANY rule exceeded\n- Headers: X-RateLimit-Limit, X-RateLimit-Remaining, X-RateLimit-Reset, Retry-After\n- Failure mode: Configurable — fail-open (allow) for non-critical APIs; fail-closed for payment APIs\n- Tiers: Load tier config on first request; cache locally with TTL refresh\n	MEDIUM	40	2026-07-25 23:56:50.233696
a9df6519-bc07-4429-97ca-3b1a75f401c0	a3000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000012	Design a Web Cache	Design a distributed caching layer (like a CDN edge cache or application cache) that sits between clients and origin servers to reduce latency and backend load.\n\n## Requirements\n\n### Functional\n- Cache HTTP responses based on URL, headers, and query parameters\n- Support cache invalidation (purge by URL, pattern, or tag)\n- Honor Cache-Control headers (max-age, no-cache, private)\n- Serve stale content while revalidating in background (stale-while-revalidate)\n- Cache warming for predictable traffic spikes\n\n### Non-Functional\n- Cache hit latency under 5ms\n- Support 1M cached objects per node\n- Cache hit ratio above 90% for cacheable content\n- Consistent hashing for cache distribution\n- Graceful origin failover on cache miss storms\n\n## Topics to Cover\n- Eviction policies (LRU, LFU, TTL-based)\n- Cache consistency and invalidation strategies\n- Thundering herd / cache stampede prevention\n- Distributed cache topology (replicated vs partitioned)\n	- 100 cache nodes, 64GB memory each\n- 1M objects per node, average object size 50KB\n- 500K requests/second across cluster\n- Cache hit ratio target: 90%+\n- Invalidation propagation: under 5 seconds cluster-wide\n	{"api_design": 15, "scalability": 20, "consistency_model": 25, "eviction_strategy": 25, "stampede_prevention": 15}	- Topology: Consistent hashing to distribute keys across nodes; virtual nodes for balance\n- Eviction: LRU with frequency boost (LFU-hybrid) — recently AND frequently accessed items survive\n- Stampede prevention: Request coalescing — first miss fetches from origin; concurrent requests wait\n- Stale-while-revalidate: Serve expired content immediately; async background refresh\n- Invalidation: Pub/sub broadcast to all nodes; tag-based purge for grouped content\n- Cache-Control: Parse response headers; respect max-age, private, no-store directives\n- Warming: Pre-fetch popular URLs before traffic spike based on schedule or prediction\n- Failure: Circuit breaker on origin; serve stale on origin timeout; shed load gracefully\n	MEDIUM	40	2026-07-25 23:56:50.23821
